# OWNER REVIEW
# Tea with three Coalition ladies on the lawn of number 4: Grizelda's test (Key 1; levels/primrose/keys/grizelda_test.gd).
# In the suit, Nim keeps her poise: each "slip" flag costs Composure, and two slips or naming the Rope and the ladies
# close ranks (blown cover). They had Grizelda to tea twelve years ago, and they still talk about it.

~ tea
[if primrose/tea_done] => had
[if not primrose/tea_set] => early
[if not primrose/in_suit] => garb
Ashby: Oh. A newcomer. Are you looking round number 4, dear?
- I'm considering it. Do sit. => one
- Um, sort of? I'm just here for the tea? => one_soft

~ one_soft
set primrose/tea_slip1
=> one

~ one
Primm: The last woman who lived there had the most peculiar visitors. Boots. Coats. At all hours.
Fairweather: We never said a word, of course.
Primm: We said a great many words. Just not to her.
- How tiresome for you. More tea? => two
- Honestly, that sounds like a great house. => two_soft

~ two_soft
set primrose/tea_slip2
=> two

~ two
Ashby: And what does your husband do, dear?
- I don't keep one. They're so much upkeep. => three
- I don't, um. I mean. There isn't. Is that bad? => three_soft
- I work at the Velvet Rope, actually. => refused

~ three_soft
[if primrose/tea_slip1 or primrose/tea_slip2] => refused
set primrose/tea_slip3
=> three

~ three
Fairweather: You'll come to Marjorie's party tonight, of course. Everyone's going. For the cause.
Primm: Decency doesn't fund itself.
- I wouldn't miss it. I hear the products are educational. => done
- What do they actually sell there? => done_soft

~ done_soft
set primrose/tea_slip3
Fairweather: Oh, you'll see. Bring a big handbag.
=> done

~ done
Ashby: Oh, she's lovely. Isn't she lovely?
Primm: Much nicer than the last one.
Fairweather: The last one made Mrs Primm cry with one look, across this very lawn.
Primm: I was not crying. I had something in my eye. For a week.
[narrator] Behind the For Sale sign, Grizelda's ears flatten, very slightly, with satisfaction.
set primrose/tea_done

~ refused
Ashby [cold]: I think we've had quite enough tea, thank you. Mrs Fairweather, ring round.
Fairweather: Ringing round.
set primrose/tea_refused
=> END

~ early
Primm: This is a private tea, dear. Residents and prospective residents only.

~ garb
Ashby: Are you the gardener? The hedges are round the back.

~ had
Ashby: Do come again, dear. Thursdays.
